description: weisssrv repo workflow, gates, and canonical-doc map — apply to every task in this repo.
alwaysApply: true
---

At the start of any task in this repository, read
`.claude/skills/weisssrv-development/SKILL.md` and follow it, then read the
`references/` file for the change-type at hand (`add-k8s-app`, `add-vm-app`,
`debugging`, `maintenance-upgrades`, `cluster-access`). It encodes the
non-negotiable workflow (branch + MR, never push `main`, no secrets in git, Flux
owns `kubernetes/`, single-source version pins), the pre-MR gate commands, and a
change-type decision tree pointing at every canonical doc. `CLAUDE.md` remains
the top-level fact source; this rule and `.cursorrules` both defer to it and to
the skill.
